   "date": "2014-09-26T08:36:56Z",
   "subject": "prior of Poisson GLMM",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Dear INLA help,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial\"><br></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&#39;Arial Unicode MS&#39;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I fitted a Poisson mixed model with a classical random effect (“iid”). The model is a little bit overdispersed. Then,</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I want to fit a classical Poisson GLMM with offset in inla. In the paper of Fong et al (2009)  they don&#39;t recommend the “<b>param=c(0.001,0.001)</b>” prior. Thus, I’d like to know which you would use. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br>In a recent paper of L. Grilli (2014) entiled ``Bayesian estimation with integrated nested Laplace approximation for binary logit mixed models&#39;&#39;, they didn’t use an inla default prior because it is very flat, and finally they used Γ (a=0.5,b=0.0164) for logistic mixed model.<br> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">My question is, which prior  would you recommend me to fit a poisson mixed model?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I think the following one could be good, but I’m not sure:</span></p><span style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br> hyper.iid &lt;- list(theta=list(prior=&quot;logtgaussian&quot;,<b>param=c(0,0.0001)</b>))<br><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Thanks in advance.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;color:black;background-image:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Martí</span></p></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dMBpB5yN0EIJ",
